= Solution
{parent=ii}

If $u=0$ on $\Sigma$ and $|\Sigma|>0$, then
$$
\int_{B_1}u_\varepsilon^{-p_0}\geq|\Sigma|\varepsilon^{-p_0}.
$$
Part (b.i) consequently gives
$$
\int_{B_1}u_\varepsilon^{p_0}leq C|\Sigma|^{-1}\varepsilon^{p_0}.
$$
Letting $\varepsilon\downarrow0$ and using <Fatou lemma> yields $\int_{B_1}u^{p_0}=0$. Since $u\geq0$ is continuous,
$$
\boxed{u\equiv0\text{ on }B_1.}
$$

